{
  "duration": 70.379,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.339,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.879,
      "end": 2.799,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.24,
      "end": 4.199,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.719,
      "end": 5.46,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.039,
      "end": 7.279,
      "text": "two centimeter of rain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.739,
      "end": 9.42,
      "text": "falls on two hectares of land,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.979,
      "end": 12.159,
      "text": "and we need to find the volume of water collected."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.619,
      "end": 14.199,
      "text": "What does this mean in simple words?"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.679,
      "end": 18.699,
      "text": "Just imagine a big field covered with a layer of water of height two centimeter."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.26,
      "end": 21.659,
      "text": "If we know the area of the field and the height of the water,"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.119,
      "end": 23.399,
      "text": "we can easily find the volume."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.039,
      "end": 29.76,
      "text": "So first, let us convert the area. We know that one hectare equal to ten thousand square meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.219,
      "end": 31.019,
      "text": "So two hectares"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.559,
      "end": 33.619,
      "text": "equal to twenty thousand square meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.259,
      "end": 34.539,
      "text": "Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.099,
      "end": 35.319,
      "text": "Now,"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.86,
      "end": 37.319,
      "text": "let us convert the rainfall."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.899,
      "end": 43.719,
      "text": "The rainfall is two centimeter, and since one hundred centimeter is equal to one meter,"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.399,
      "end": 47.7,
      "text": "two centimeter equal to zero point zero two meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.139,
      "end": 48.379,
      "text": "Okay,"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.719,
      "end": 50.86,
      "text": "now both values are in the correct units."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.579,
      "end": 54.899,
      "text": "Now we have volume equal to area into height."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.34,
      "end": 62.639,
      "text": "So volume equal to twenty thousand into zero point zero two. After solving this, we get four hundred cubic meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.5,
      "end": 64.779,
      "text": "Done and dusted."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.22,
      "end": 67.659,
      "text": "So the final answer will be four hundred cubic meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.119,
      "end": 68.479,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.979,
      "end": 70.379,
      "text": "option B is the correct answer."
    }
  ],
